From 08ecfa1fbd90b84c72095a44abc55c1fac484d41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Techniix <54037125+Techniix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:31:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kernel/x86_64: Add LDT and custom FS support for 32 bit code

Running 32 bit code in compatibility mode inside a 64 bit team (as
Wine's WoW64 does) needs a way to set up data segments and to point FS
at something other than the TLS block. Add two calls to the "thread"
generic syscall subsystem:

* THREAD_SET_LDT installs entries in a per-team local descriptor table.
  Only user mode code and data descriptors are accepted. The table is
  loaded through a per-CPU GDT slot on context switch.
* THREAD_SET_FS_BASE sets the FS base of the calling thread.

Once a team has used either, the FS selector and FS base of its threads
are saved and restored on context switches, and passed in the signal
context (new fs and fs_base fields in the FXSAVE software area).

Signal handlers now always run in 64 bit mode with FS pointing at the
TLS, and returning from a signal handler can resume either 64 or 32 bit
user code.
